.DS_Store

# Screenshots. `F12` writes them into the working directory, and so does
# `FLY_CAPTURE` unless it is pointed somewhere else. They are how the build gets
# looked at, not part of it.
/fly-*.png
/*.png

# Opificium's project sits BESIDE the assets rather than inside them: the asset
# folder is copied verbatim into the shipped bundle, and `file_watcher` has the
# running game watching it, so a bench autosaving in there would both ship the
# workshop and reload the game mid-write. `install` in opificium.json carries
# finished work across to assets/buildings, which is the version the game reads.
#
# The blueprints under out/buildings ARE tracked — they are the floor plan's
# source and 26 KB of very diffable JSON. What is not tracked is the bake's
# own intermediate output, which is regenerated from them.
/opificium/out/baked/
